Subject: [PATCH] test-build: declare the exported DWC allocator with debug locks

The pinned vendor source defines and exports DWC_SPINLOCK_ALLOC even with
CONFIG_DEBUG_SPINLOCK. Move its existing declaration outside the conditional;
leave call-site debug allocation macros and all function statements unchanged.
Separate isolated diagnostic build overlay, not part of the production series.

--- a/drivers/usb/host/dwc_common_port/dwc_os.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/dwc_common_port/dwc_os.h
@@ -1046,2 +1046,3 @@
  * makes it falsely think recursive locking occurs. */
+extern dwc_spinlock_t *DWC_SPINLOCK_ALLOC(void);
 #if defined(DWC_LINUX) && defined(CONFIG_DEBUG_SPINLOCK)
@@ -1054,3 +1055,2 @@
 #else
-extern dwc_spinlock_t *DWC_SPINLOCK_ALLOC(void);
 #define dwc_spinlock_alloc(_ctx_) DWC_SPINLOCK_ALLOC()
